<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Bae Jung-son</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. <a href="/years/1271">1271</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Bae Jung-son was a Goryeo military officer who led the Sambyeolcho units in revolt in 1270, when the court returned to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kaesong">Kaegyong</a> and accepted Mongol overlordship. The rebels proclaimed the royal kinsman <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wang-on">Wang On</a> as king and sailed to Jindo island, where they built the Yongjang fortress. A Goryeo and Mongol army stormed Jindo in 1271, and Bae Jung-son is believed to have died there.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/bae-jung-son.jpg" alt="Bae Jung-son" width="320" height="569" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Jangg8962 · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:%EB%B0%B0%EC%A4%91%EC%86%90_%EC%82%AC%EB%8B%B9_%EB%8F%99%EC%83%81.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
